/**
\page ex_hello Hello Janus

<p class="lede">The smallest program that puts something on screen: a camera, a light, a background and one sprite.</p>

<div class="jd-meta"><span><b>Source</b> \exsrc{modules/HelloJanus.cpp}</span><span><b>Executable</b> <code>HelloJanus</code></span><span><b>Module</b> \ref engine_core</span></div>

\image html hello-janus.png "The orange square, with the engine's FPS Counter, Entity Debugger and Dear ImGui Demo windows"

This is the program walked through in \ref first_game. It shows the four things every Janus game needs before anything is visible (\ref essentials_minimum) and the order of the engine calls (\ref engine_core).

## Textures without files

\genexopen{modules/HelloJanus.cpp,Registering a texture made in code}
\snippet modules/HelloJanus.cpp solid_texture
\endex

## main()

\genexopen{modules/HelloJanus.cpp,main()}
\snippet modules/HelloJanus.cpp main
\endex

The program ends with `std::quick_exit(0)` instead of returning, to avoid the crash after shutdown described in \ref known_issues_shutdown.
*/

/**
\page ex_logging Logging

<p class="lede">A console program that declares loggers in three different ways and writes messages at each level. It opens no window and starts only the Log module.</p>

<div class="jd-meta"><span><b>Source</b> \exsrc{modules/Logging.cpp}</span><span><b>Executable</b> <code>LoggingExample</code></span><span><b>Module</b> \ref logging</span></div>

## Declaring loggers

\genexopen{modules/Logging.cpp,Three ways to get a logger}
\snippet modules/Logging.cpp declare
\snippet modules/Logging.cpp declare_params
\snippet modules/Logging.cpp manual
\endex

## Logging

\genexopen{modules/Logging.cpp,Starting the module and logging at every level}
\snippet modules/Logging.cpp module
\snippet modules/Logging.cpp levels
\snippet modules/Logging.cpp other_loggers
\snippet modules/Logging.cpp teardown
\endex

## Output

The console shows (times will differ):

```
[11/22/26 16:30:57] [LogInventory] error: Item 42 is missing from the database
[11/22/26 16:30:57] [LogInventory] warning: Inventory is 90% full
[11/22/26 16:30:57] [LogInventory] info: Picked up 3 x apple
[11/22/26 16:30:57] [LogInventory] debug: Slots used: 7/20
[11/22/26 16:30:57] [LogGeneric] info: The generic logger needs no declaration
[11/22/26 16:30:57] [LogAudio] warning: Sound jump.wav is missing
```

- The `Verbose` message is missing: trace messages are below the global level the Log module sets.
- `LogNetwork` writes nothing to the console. Its message is in `Logs/Network.log` next to the executable.
- The `LogAudio` info message is missing: that logger only writes warnings and errors.
- After `Log::TeardownModule()`, the `Logs` folder also holds timestamped copies such as `JanusEngine-2026-11-22-h21m30.log` (the time in the name is UTC).

## Full source

\genex{modules/Logging.cpp,Logging.cpp}
\include modules/Logging.cpp
\endex
*/

/**
\page ex_input Input

<p class="lede">Every kind of input binding in one place: a square you move with the arrow keys, three lights for Space's press, hold and release bindings, a key combination, a callback and quitting with Escape.</p>

<div class="jd-meta"><span><b>Source</b> \exsrc{modules/Input.cpp}</span><span><b>Executable</b> <code>InputExample</code></span><span><b>Module</b> \ref input</span></div>

\image html input.png "The release light (right) glows just after Space was let go; the HUD shows the action values"

| Key | Action | Binding |
| --- | --- | --- |
| Arrow keys | `Move` (`glm::vec2`, `ADD`) | Hold |
| <kbd>Shift</kbd> | `SpeedBoost` (`float`, `OVERRIDE`) | Hold |
| <kbd>Space</kbd> | `SpacePressed`, `SpaceHeld`, `SpaceReleased` | Press, hold, release |
| <kbd>Ctrl</kbd> + <kbd>S</kbd> | `Save` | Hold, two keys |
| <kbd>Enter</kbd> | `Confirm`, with a callback | Press |
| <kbd>Esc</kbd> | `Quit` | Press |

## Declaring and binding

\genexopen{modules/Input.cpp,Actions}
\snippet modules/Input.cpp actions
\endex

\genexopen{modules/Input.cpp,Bindings}
\snippet modules/Input.cpp bindings
\endex

## Reading actions

\genexopen{modules/Input.cpp,Polling in a system}
\snippet modules/Input.cpp polling
\endex

\genexopen{modules/Input.cpp,A callback}
\snippet modules/Input.cpp callback
\endex

## Quitting from code

\genexopen{modules/Input.cpp,Escape pushes a quit event}
\snippet modules/Input.cpp quit
\endex

## Full source

\genex{modules/Input.cpp,Input.cpp}
\include modules/Input.cpp
\endex
