/**
\page ex_assets Assets and memory

<p class="lede">What the Filesystem module finds, how to load and cache assets, how to add your own asset type, how to make a texture in code, and how TObjectPtr behaves.</p>

<div class="jd-meta"><span><b>Source</b> \exsrc{modules/AssetsAndMemory.cpp}</span><span><b>Executable</b> <code>AssetsExample</code></span><span><b>Modules</b> \ref filesystem, \ref memory</span></div>

\image html assets.png "The Asset Browser tool lists every registered asset; the checkerboard is a texture generated at runtime"

Most of this example writes to the log. Its output looks like this (paths shortened):

```
[LogAssets] info: 13 assets registered
[LogAssets] info: Shader asset: Shaders\Compiled\LightShader.vert
...
[LogAssets] info: Name: PullSpriteBatch.vert  Extension: .dxil  File: ...\Resources\Shaders\Compiled\PullSpriteBatch.vert.dxil
[LogAssets] info: FragmentShaderSrc.frag is 294 characters long. First line: Texture2D<float4> Texture : register(t0, space2);
[LogAssets] info: Cached: true
[LogAssets] info: VertexShaderSrc.vert has 79 lines
[LogAssets] info: Generated\Checker valid: true
[LogAssets] info: Items: 3 (both pointers see 3)
[LogAssets] info: empty.IsValid() = false
[LogAssets] info: After Clear: inventory valid = true, sameInventory valid = false
[LogAssets] info: CastTo round trip: hello
```

## Finding assets

\genexopen{modules/AssetsAndMemory.cpp,Listing and looking up}
\snippet modules/AssetsAndMemory.cpp listing
\snippet modules/AssetsAndMemory.cpp asset_data
\endex

Note `Extension: .dxil`: the shader has three files with the same name, and only the first one found is registered (\ref filesystem_paths).

## Loading

\genexopen{modules/AssetsAndMemory.cpp,Loading text\, and the cache}
\snippet modules/AssetsAndMemory.cpp load_text
\endex

\genexopen{modules/AssetsAndMemory.cpp,A custom asset type}
